# FauxBuild diagnostic palette v1 — original content.
# 16 ramps of 16 entries each; every entry defined; components are 6-bit.

palette diagnostic

# Ramp 0: neutral gray ramp (indices 0..15) — shade-table anchor.
ramp 0 16 0 0 0 -> 60 60 60
# Ramp 1: red ramp (16..31).
ramp 16 16 0 0 0 -> 60 0 0
# Ramp 2: green (32..47).
ramp 32 16 0 0 0 -> 0 60 0
# Ramp 3: blue (48..63).
ramp 48 16 0 0 0 -> 0 0 60
# Ramp 4: cyan (64..79).
ramp 64 16 0 0 0 -> 0 60 60
# Ramp 5: magenta (80..95).
ramp 80 16 0 0 0 -> 60 0 60
# Ramp 6: yellow (96..111).
ramp 96 16 0 0 0 -> 60 60 0
# Ramp 7: brown (112..127).
ramp 112 16 0 0 0 -> 40 24 8
# Ramp 8: warm white (128..143).
ramp 128 16 8 6 4 -> 62 60 58
# Ramp 9: cool white (144..159).
ramp 144 16 4 6 8 -> 58 60 62
# Ramp 10: orange (160..175).
ramp 160 16 0 0 0 -> 60 32 0
# Ramp 11: teal (176..191).
ramp 176 16 0 0 0 -> 0 32 32
# Ramp 12: violet (192..207).
ramp 192 16 0 0 0 -> 32 0 60
# Ramp 13: olive (208..223).
ramp 208 16 0 0 0 -> 32 32 0
# Ramp 14: slate (224..239).
ramp 224 16 8 10 14 -> 40 44 52
# Ramp 15: error magenta/white hazard (240..255) — unmissable in any misuse.
ramp 240 8 60 0 60 -> 62 62 62
ramp 248 8 62 62 62 -> 60 0 60

# Sprite palette swaps (LOOKUP.DAT): tint blends snapped to nearest entries.
swap 1 tint 60 0 0
swap 2 tint 0 60 0
swap 3 tint 0 0 60
swap 4 tint 60 60 0

shades 32
translucent on
